  <h2>Notice and repair form or narrative viewpoint</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="went" data-hint="Had requires the participle of go, not its Past Simple form." data-fix="When Maya called at 8:20, the driver had gone." data-why="Gone is the past participle in go, went, gone. The 8:20 call supplies the later past reference point." data-success-message="Correct. Gone is the participle required after had for the earlier departure.">
    <h3>Repair 1: use the participle</h3><p>Tap the verb form that breaks <span class="ex">had + past participle</span>.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="when">When</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="maya">Maya</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="called">called at 8:20,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="driver">the driver</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="had">had</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="went">went.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="didn’t had" data-hint="The sentence asks for an earlier lack of time before the 9:00 opening, so put the negative on had and keep had as the participle of have." data-fix="Before the doors opened at 9:00, I hadn’t had time to test microphone three." data-why="Past Perfect negative is hadn’t + past participle. The lexical verb have also has the participle had, producing hadn’t had." data-success-message="Correct. Hadn’t had accurately marks the earlier lack of time before the 9:00 opening.">
    <h3>Repair 2: build the negative earlier layer</h3><p>Tap the two-word form that cannot follow the stated earlier-time context.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="before">Before</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="doors">the doors opened at 9:00,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="didn’t had">didn’t had</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="time">time</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="test">to test microphone three.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="had opened" data-hint="These three main-story events are explicitly told in the order they happened; no backward layer is needed." data-fix="At 5:50, Maya unlocked the doors, opened them, and welcomed the guests." data-why="Past Simple moves a chronological main story forward. Past Perfect is not a general marker for every event that happened in the past." data-success-message="Correct. Opened belongs on the chronological Past Simple story line, so the unnecessary had must go.">
    <h3>Repair 3: remove unnecessary backshifting</h3><p>Tap the verb phrase that incorrectly turns one chronological action into a flashback.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="time">At 5:50,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="maya">Maya</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="unlocked">unlocked the doors,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="had opened">had opened them,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="welcomed">and welcomed the guests.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it without exposing private history</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose a real employer, client, mistake, password, travel problem, family event, relationship, health issue, financial detail, address, schedule, or personal history. Use the fictional Harbor forum. Real details are optional.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Delivery problem:</b> Maya arrived at 8:15. The driver left at 8:10, and someone moved the boxes earlier. Explain what Maya discovered and why.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Schedule problem:</b> At 4:45, Hall B was empty because nobody updated the schedule after the tables moved. Move from the main discovery to the earlier cause.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Successful recovery:</b> By 5:05, Maya confirmed the mistake and arranged carts. Then the team moved, tested, and opened. Mark the deadline, then return to the main story.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Prior experience:</b> Invent a coordinator who had never led a forum before 2025 but had organized three smaller meetings. Contrast no experience in one area with completed experience in another.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: reconstruct a 75–90 second fictional event</h3>
    <p>Use one Harbor scenario. Establish the main past scene, add one completed earlier event, one earlier cause, and either prior experience or a state up to that past point. Include one negative or question. Return clearly to the main Past Simple story and finish with the result.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener identify the main past reference point, every earlier layer, the reason for each Past Perfect choice, and the exact moment when the story returns to Past Simple?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You protected the past reference point, used Past Perfect only for a meaningful earlier layer, and returned to Past Simple for the main narrative.">
