    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="When Maya arrived at 8:15, the driver had already left at 8:10." data-hint="The later arrival is mentioned first, so use Past Perfect for the earlier 8:10 departure." data-fix="When Maya arrived at 8:15, the driver had already left at 8:10."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which sentence makes the reversed order explicit?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When Maya arrived at 8:15, the driver had already left at 8:10.">When Maya arrived at 8:15, the driver had already left at 8:10.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When Maya will arrive, the driver leaves yesterday.">When Maya will arrive, the driver leaves yesterday.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="When Maya had arrive, the driver had lefts.">When Maya had arrive, the driver had lefts.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The boxes were missing because someone had moved them to Hall A." data-hint="Use Past Perfect for the movement that caused the later missing-box problem." data-fix="The boxes were missing because someone had moved them to Hall A."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence gives an earlier cause for a later past result?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The boxes were missing because someone had moved them to Hall A.">The boxes were missing because someone had moved them to Hall A.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The boxes are missing because someone will moved them.">The boxes are missing because someone will moved them.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The boxes had missing because someone moves them now.">The boxes had missing because someone moves them now.</button></div></div>
