        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Both are possible; had checked more deliberately views the check as complete from the later call." data-hint="Before already makes the order clear, so compare viewpoint rather than labeling one grammatical version wrong." data-fix="Both are possible; had checked more deliberately views the check as complete from the later call."><p class="quiz-question">2. Compare <span class="ex">Maya checked the list before she called</span> and <span class="ex">Maya had checked the list before she called</span>. Which explanation is accurate?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both are possible; had checked more deliberately views the check as complete from the later call.">Both are possible; had checked more deliberately views the check as complete from the later call.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Only Past Perfect is ever grammatical with before.">Only Past Perfect is ever grammatical with before.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Both sentences describe future events.">Both sentences describe future events.</button></div></div>
